WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.870 --> 00:00:06.190
Hello, everyone, and welcome to your second drink of The Duel.

2
00:00:06.550 --> 00:00:10.030
This might be one of my all-time favorite episodes of The Office.

3
00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:12.310
I know I say that so often.

4
00:00:12.310 --> 00:00:15.030
I also just really happen to like season five.

5
00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:17.210
Yeah, it's really solid.

6
00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:20.930
Well, there's just so many great moments in The Duel.

7
00:00:21.170 --> 00:00:24.190
I love the Andy and Dwight duel over Angela,

8
00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:27.810
but there's also all the scenes with Michael and David Wallace in New York.

9
00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:32.690
I'm very curious to hear what the fan favorite moment of this episode was.

10
00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:34.850
Well, we got this letter from Melissa Kay.

11
00:00:35.270 --> 00:00:36.050
Melissa says,

12
00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:36.790
Hi, ladies.

13
00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:38.330
Absolutely love your show.

14
00:00:38.490 --> 00:00:43.350
And one of my absolute favorite scenes from the whole show is at 10 minutes and 53 seconds

15
00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:47.550
when Michael is talking about his philosophy to David Wallace and says,

16
00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:53.730
Don't ever, for any reason, do anything to anyone for any reason.

17
00:00:54.130 --> 00:00:56.710
It goes on and on with this line.

18
00:00:56.710 --> 00:01:01.110
I love this line so much and it completely captures the moment when you're asked a question

19
00:01:01.110 --> 00:01:04.030
you don't know the answer to and you have to make it up as you go.

20
00:01:04.370 --> 00:01:06.290
Was all of that improvised or was

21
00:01:06.290 --> 00:01:07.210
it fully scripted?

22
00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:08.150
Thanks, Melissa.

23
00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:11.050
Okay, so Melissa, we talked about this in our breakdown,

24
00:01:11.350 --> 00:01:14.910
how Steve improvised a lot of this, but we didn't play it.

25
00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:16.630
And I pulled a clip from the

26
00:01:16.630 --> 00:01:21.010
superfan version because there is an extra joke at the top and it really cracked us up.

27
00:01:21.010 --> 00:01:22.430
Let's hear it.

28
00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:26.290
My philosophy is basically this.

29
00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:31.430
I like to sell paper for more than I bought the paper for.

30
00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:33.490
That's obviously obvious.

31
00:01:33.650 --> 00:01:36.810
But here's the thing, and this is something that I live by,

32
00:01:37.050 --> 00:01:39.510
and I always have, and I always will.

33
00:01:40.790 --> 00:01:46.490
Don't ever, for any reason, do anything to anyone,

34
00:01:46.490 --> 00:01:55.890
for any reason ever no matter what no matter where or who or who you are with

35
00:01:57.050 --> 00:02:08.380
or or where you are going or or where you've been ever for any reason

36
00:02:08.380 --> 00:02:11.900
whatsoever sometimes I'll start a sentence and I don't even know where it's

37
00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:18.140
going I just hope I find it along the way like an improv conversation an

38
00:02:18.140 --> 00:02:18.980
improvisation.

39
00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:22.800
I mean, it's something he lives by and always will.

40
00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:24.540
For any reason.

41
00:02:24.940 --> 00:02:26.020
For any reason.

42
00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:32.120
So not only was this our fan favorite moment of the episode, we also got a letter that this scene

43
00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:33.160
is educational.

44
00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:35.180
Listen to this.

45
00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:36.440
Angela B.

46
00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:39.820
wrote in and said, more of a comment for this episode.

47
00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:44.360
I taught English 101 at a university which focused on college writing.

48
00:02:44.840 --> 00:02:45.840
Every semester,

49
00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:49.000
whenever I did a lesson on needing to have a purpose for writing,

50
00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:51.420
I would show the clip from this episode

51
00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:54.320
where Michael starts to answer David Wallace's question

52
00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:56.800
and later says that he doesn't always know

53
00:02:56.800 --> 00:02:58.520
where his sentences are going to go.

54
00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:01.180
It's a great example about how

55
00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:04.620
if you don't know what the point of your argument or statement is,

56
00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:06.660
you'll end up with meandering thoughts.

57
00:03:06.860 --> 00:03:07.940
That's so wonderful.

58
00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:09.460
Hey, you know what?

59
00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:10.860
Just get it down on paper.

60
00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:12.060
You'll find it, right?

61
00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:18.360
Well, Angela, you might remember that I got really into the subject of dueling

62
00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:20.740
when we did this episode.

63
00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:24.340
Yes, I did a little deep dive on the rules of dueling.

64
00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:28.960
Well, we got some mail from folks that took my dive even deeper.

65
00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:31.860
And I'm going to read two letters that really tickled me.

66
00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:34.940
The first is from Laura H., who said,

67
00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:38.780
Hi, I really enjoyed the dual podcast episode.

68
00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:41.180
To add to your discussion of dueling,

69
00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:46.660
I wanted you to know that as an attorney in Kentucky, I had to be sworn in by the state

70
00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:47.580
Supreme Court.

71
00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:54.420
As part of the swearing-in process, attorneys have to solemnly swear, quote, that since the

72
00:03:54.420 --> 00:04:00.780
adoption of the present Constitution, I, being a citizen of this state, have not fought

73
00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:07.060
a duel with deadly weapons within this state, nor out of it, nor have I sent or accepted

74
00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:12.560
a challenge to fight a duel with deadly weapons, nor have I acted as a second in carrying a

75
00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:16.200
challenge, nor aided or assisted any person thus offending.

76
00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:18.520
My goodness.

77
00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:23.980
Laura said the discussion regarding dueling is nearly half of the entire oath.

78
00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:25.980
That's bonkers.

79
00:04:25.980 --> 00:04:29.080
It was really funny to say that during the ceremony.

80
00:04:29.320 --> 00:04:30.900
And then Nicole C.

81
00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:31.880
wrote in to say,

82
00:04:32.060 --> 00:04:36.320
I enjoyed hearing your history of dueling and wanted to let you know something else.

83
00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:43.480
I am a lawyer in the military, a JAG, and the military has its own set of rules called

84
00:04:43.480 --> 00:04:47.880
the Uniform Code of Military Justice, or UCMJ.

85
00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:51.580
There is an article in the UCMJ article 114

86
00:04:51.580 --> 00:04:58.480
that makes it illegal for military members to duel, to promote a duel, to not take action in

87
00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:01.820
stopping a duel, or to fail to report a duel.

88
00:05:02.020 --> 00:05:03.420
So no dueling again.

89
00:05:03.580 --> 00:05:06.100
But then Nicole goes on to say,

90
00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:09.900
that when we prepare to court-martial someone,

91
00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:13.480
they have models of the argument that they make.

92
00:05:13.940 --> 00:05:16.000
And Nicole said,

93
00:05:16.220 --> 00:05:18.860
if we were going to court-martial Andy for dueling,

94
00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:21.020
here is how that would be argued.

95
00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:22.180
Quote,

96
00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:27.080
in that Andy Bernard did at or near the Scranton Business Park

97
00:05:27.080 --> 00:05:28.600
on or about this date,

98
00:05:28.920 --> 00:05:30.600
fight a duel with Dwight Schrute

99
00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:33.800
using as a weapon, therefore, a Toyota Prius.

100
00:05:35.980 --> 00:05:41.180
but nicole says there could also be a court-martial for angela for promoting a duel

101
00:05:41.180 --> 00:05:47.880
and it would sound like this in that angela martin did at or near the scranton business park on or

102
00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:52.660
about this date promote a duel between dwight shrewd and andy bernard by telling andy he would

103
00:05:52.660 --> 00:06:01.740
be a coward if he failed to challenge dwight to a duel so two sets of charges i guess though

104
00:06:01.740 --> 00:06:03.700
maybe Dwight should be charged as well.

105
00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:04.560
He did participate.

106
00:06:04.900 --> 00:06:06.560
I found that all fascinating.

107
00:06:06.980 --> 00:06:07.400
I mean,

108
00:06:07.780 --> 00:06:10.240
people had a lot of thoughts on dueling.

109
00:06:10.420 --> 00:06:12.220
Dueling was like a big deal.

110
00:06:12.540 --> 00:06:13.100
Big deal.

111
00:06:13.360 --> 00:06:14.120
Well, listen,

112
00:06:14.320 --> 00:06:16.920
everyone, thank you for tuning in.

113
00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:18.140
Thank you for writing in.

114
00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:19.580
Please write us your fan favorite

115
00:06:19.580 --> 00:06:23.320
moments over in our second drinks folder at officeladies.com.

116
00:06:23.480 --> 00:06:25.300
And now please enjoy the duel,

117
00:06:25.460 --> 00:06:26.420
but don't do a duel.

118
00:06:26.640 --> 00:06:27.000
No.

119
00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:31.360
And we've got really great tidbits in this one too from Jen Salata,

120
00:06:31.360 --> 00:06:33.700
director Dean Holland and producer Randy Cordray.

121
00:06:33.880 --> 00:06:34.840
So go give it a listen.

122
00:06:39.630 --> 00:06:40.210
I'm Jenna Fisher.

123
00:06:40.390 --> 00:06:40.810
And I'm

124
00:06:40.810 --> 00:06:41.510
Angela Kinsey.

125
00:06:41.650 --> 00:06:42.790
We were on The Office together.

126
00:06:43.050 --> 00:06:44.050
And we're best friends.

127
00:06:44.150 --> 00:06:45.070
And now we're doing the

128
00:06:45.070 --> 00:06:47.870
Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.

129
00:06:48.030 --> 00:06:50.010
Each week, we will break down an episode of

130
00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:54.450
The Office and give exclusive behind the scenes stories that only two people who were there can

131
00:06:54.450 --> 00:06:54.850
tell you.

132
00:06:55.070 --> 00:06:56.010
We're The Office Ladies.

133
00:06:59.650 --> 00:07:01.070
Lady, it's the duel.

134
00:07:01.530 --> 00:07:03.430
I mean, two men are going to fight over

135
00:07:03.430 --> 00:07:04.410
me today.

136
00:07:05.850 --> 00:07:07.010
Me, a.k.a.

137
00:07:07.170 --> 00:07:07.970
Angela Martin.

138
00:07:08.330 --> 00:07:12.550
I have to say, like Andy's Prius, this episode sneaked

139
00:07:12.550 --> 00:07:14.930
up on me, but in a great way.

140
00:07:15.430 --> 00:07:16.770
Oh, my gosh, Hidden Gem.

141
00:07:17.050 --> 00:07:18.130
It's so good.

142
00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:19.110
It's one of my favorite

143
00:07:19.110 --> 00:07:19.570
episodes.

144
00:07:19.850 --> 00:07:21.010
I loved watching it.

145
00:07:21.090 --> 00:07:22.150
I loved filming it.

146
00:07:22.270 --> 00:07:23.790
And I'm excited to talk about it today.

147
00:07:24.030 --> 00:07:30.190
Well, it is season five, episode 12, written by Jen Salata and directed by Dean Holland.

148
00:07:30.850 --> 00:07:31.650
Here's your summary.

149
00:07:31.910 --> 00:07:36.570
Michael takes it upon himself to expose Angela and Dwight's affair to Andy.

150
00:07:36.950 --> 00:07:40.890
The two men then challenge one another to a duel in the parking lot.

151
00:07:41.110 --> 00:07:45.250
Meanwhile, Michael is summoned to corporate to speak with David Wallace.

152
00:07:45.670 --> 00:07:50.610
He thinks it's going to be bad news, but he gets some unexpected praise.

153
00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:52.870
Oh, those scenes.

154
00:07:52.890 --> 00:07:55.390
We'll get to it, but man, those are good too.

155
00:07:55.950 --> 00:07:57.410
Fast fact number one.

156
00:07:57.930 --> 00:08:01.970
This episode was written by the always amazing Jen Salata.

157
00:08:02.550 --> 00:08:03.650
Applause for Jen!

158
00:08:03.970 --> 00:08:04.670
Oh, Jen.

159
00:08:05.150 --> 00:08:08.150
Jen, so many good lines in this.

160
00:08:08.410 --> 00:08:15.650
I reached out to Jen, and she sent in an audio clip explaining the inspiration behind this episode.

161
00:08:15.930 --> 00:08:16.910
Let's hear it.

162
00:08:17.350 --> 00:08:21.970
My biggest memory about writing The Duel was how little I had when I was sent off to write the script.

163
00:08:22.390 --> 00:08:26.510
It was mid-season five, and it was a really busy patch for the writers, for all of us.

164
00:08:26.510 --> 00:08:29.790
And I remember this episode had to be written really, really quickly.

165
00:08:29.950 --> 00:08:33.630
And I knew it was about Andy finding out about Angela and Dwight's affair.

166
00:08:33.950 --> 00:08:38.670
But where we'd usually spend time as a group fleshing out the story, I went off on this

167
00:08:38.670 --> 00:08:39.630
script with a sentence.

168
00:08:40.310 --> 00:08:44.570
Andy runs over Dwight in his Prius, keeping it under five miles an hour so Dwight doesn't

169
00:08:44.570 --> 00:08:45.150
hear him coming.

170
00:08:45.470 --> 00:08:48.910
I mean, it was a good sentence, but there was a lot to fill in.

171
00:08:49.070 --> 00:08:49.930
That was it.

172
00:08:50.070 --> 00:08:50.890
She had a sentence.

173
00:08:51.230 --> 00:08:53.550
And she crafted this amazing story.

174
00:08:53.810 --> 00:08:54.150
Yes.

175
00:08:54.150 --> 00:08:57.750
why Andi was going to run over Dwight slowly with a Prius.

176
00:08:58.190 --> 00:08:59.290
She didn't know.

177
00:08:59.530 --> 00:09:00.450
She just knew

178
00:09:00.450 --> 00:09:01.990
that was going to happen in the episode.

179
00:09:02.210 --> 00:09:03.790
And this is what she came up with.

180
00:09:03.930 --> 00:09:05.630
She had to build to that moment.

181
00:09:05.990 --> 00:09:09.010
Because usually they would get whole outlines.

182
00:09:09.310 --> 00:09:12.770
They would have an A plot, a B plot, all of it.

183
00:09:13.030 --> 00:09:13.550
No.

184
00:09:14.070 --> 00:09:14.530
Amazing.

185
00:09:14.830 --> 00:09:15.830
Jen Salata, again.

186
00:09:16.270 --> 00:09:17.210
Applause, Jen.

187
00:09:17.370 --> 00:09:17.690
Amazing.

188
00:09:18.910 --> 00:09:23.070
Fast fact number two, this episode was directed by Dean Holland.

189
00:09:23.070 --> 00:09:26.970
And Dean was our other editor alongside Dave Rogers.

190
00:09:27.370 --> 00:09:28.410
We love Dean.

191
00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:32.450
Yes, we love Dean, and he knew the show so well, much like Dave.

192
00:09:32.630 --> 00:09:34.310
They knew every moment.

193
00:09:34.630 --> 00:09:34.990
Oh, yeah.

194
00:09:35.370 --> 00:09:41.230
Dean told me that he had directed something for MTV, but that this was his first time directing

195
00:09:41.230 --> 00:09:42.950
an episode of television.

196
00:09:43.290 --> 00:09:47.430
He was so nervous that he threw up in the bathroom at Crew Call.

197
00:09:47.630 --> 00:09:48.670
Aw, Dean.

198
00:09:49.310 --> 00:09:51.610
When he texted me that, I was like, are you joking?

199
00:09:51.610 --> 00:09:53.290
He said, no, I'm being serious.

200
00:09:53.290 --> 00:09:54.850
I vomited in the bathroom.

201
00:09:56.190 --> 00:10:01.190
He said that it was really daunting because he had come from editing and he hadn't spent

202
00:10:01.190 --> 00:10:03.310
a lot of time on set.

203
00:10:03.670 --> 00:10:06.230
You know, an editor's life is very isolating.

204
00:10:06.410 --> 00:10:07.750
They're just in their editing room.

205
00:10:07.850 --> 00:10:12.370
And while we would pop over and say hello, it's very different than how a set works.

206
00:10:12.530 --> 00:10:16.150
And he said he felt a little bit like a stranger in a strange land.

207
00:10:16.350 --> 00:10:17.390
Those were his words.

208
00:10:18.090 --> 00:10:21.190
But he also said he'd consulted a little bit with Paul Feig.

209
00:10:21.510 --> 00:10:25.830
But more than anything, he did a ton of prep work for this episode.

210
00:10:26.330 --> 00:10:28.450
He said he knew the script inside and out.

211
00:10:28.570 --> 00:10:29.610
And listen to this.

212
00:10:29.810 --> 00:10:32.630
He said it changed very little from our table read.

213
00:10:33.010 --> 00:10:36.990
So that was good because he had been prepping and prepping on that table read draft.

214
00:10:37.370 --> 00:10:43.030
And a lot of times, you know, after the table read, they'll come back and the whole scenes are gone and new plots.

215
00:10:43.230 --> 00:10:43.890
But no.

216
00:10:44.010 --> 00:10:44.370
Oh, yeah.

217
00:10:44.530 --> 00:10:47.110
He said he was really happy that not a lot changed.

218
00:10:47.390 --> 00:10:52.450
But I think, again, Jen Salata clearly nailed this one from the beginning.

219
00:10:52.710 --> 00:10:53.930
She nailed it.

220
00:10:54.170 --> 00:10:57.390
So here's a little secret that Randy Cordray told me, Angela.

221
00:10:57.610 --> 00:11:02.970
You know, he's our line producer, and he's in charge of setting the schedule for the directors.

222
00:11:03.390 --> 00:11:06.450
Yeah, so he must have known when Dean was directing.

223
00:11:06.730 --> 00:11:11.850
He manipulated the schedule so that Dean would get this episode,

224
00:11:11.850 --> 00:11:15.770
because when he read it, he thought Dean would be perfect to direct it.

225
00:11:15.770 --> 00:11:17.310
Oh, my gosh.

226
00:11:17.470 --> 00:11:18.770
Randy, look at you.

227
00:11:18.970 --> 00:11:19.350
I know.

228
00:11:19.350 --> 00:11:19.690
Working it.

229
00:11:19.990 --> 00:11:20.190
Yeah.

230
00:11:20.390 --> 00:11:24.430
He said he really wanted Dean to get this one for his directorial debut.

231
00:11:24.690 --> 00:11:26.450
I mean, what a gift.

232
00:11:27.210 --> 00:11:27.650
Wow.

233
00:11:28.130 --> 00:11:33.150
Well, this was a really big episode, you know, for the whole love triangle, the Dwight, Andy,

234
00:11:33.270 --> 00:11:33.610
Angela.

235
00:11:33.990 --> 00:11:34.950
It was all coming to a head.

236
00:11:35.070 --> 00:11:37.610
And I was nervous, actually, about this episode.

237
00:11:37.770 --> 00:11:40.630
I just knew that I wanted to play these moments right.

238
00:11:40.750 --> 00:11:45.750
And it was a tricky kind of scenario, Jenna, because it's like Angela is worried about

239
00:11:45.750 --> 00:11:47.410
both of them and feeling guilt.

240
00:11:47.610 --> 00:11:50.130
But also, I don't know, is she turned on?

241
00:11:50.370 --> 00:11:51.010
I don't know.

242
00:11:51.250 --> 00:11:52.470
There's a lot happening.

243
00:11:52.670 --> 00:11:56.450
And I felt very safe knowing Dean was directing me this week

244
00:11:56.450 --> 00:11:58.090
because we knew him.

245
00:11:58.270 --> 00:11:58.930
You know what I mean?

246
00:11:59.070 --> 00:12:00.930
And I could go up to him and be like, Dean,

247
00:12:01.170 --> 00:12:01.950
did I do that right?

248
00:12:01.950 --> 00:12:02.650
What do you think?

249
00:12:02.790 --> 00:12:03.690
Should I try something else?

250
00:12:03.870 --> 00:12:05.950
So I felt very happy to have

251
00:12:05.950 --> 00:12:07.730
Dean there for the duel.

252
00:12:08.370 --> 00:12:12.050
Well, shortly after this, he went over to do Parks and Rec.

253
00:12:12.270 --> 00:12:12.830
He was

