01:01:32.070 --> 01:01:33.010
I would watch it.

1328
01:01:33.190 --> 01:01:34.450
I would do, actually.

1329
01:01:34.770 --> 01:01:36.050
They're probably amazing.

1330
01:01:36.810 --> 01:01:43.530
Well, we got a lot of questions about how did we do this scene?

1331
01:01:43.670 --> 01:01:45.110
How did we do this stunt?

1332
01:01:45.310 --> 01:01:46.530
Who was driving?

1333
01:01:47.230 --> 01:01:48.450
Yada, yada.

1334
01:01:48.710 --> 01:01:56.070
Well, I talked to Dean and he said this was really complicated because we had to shoot

1335
01:01:56.070 --> 01:02:01.430
this scene over two different days from three different locations.

1336
01:02:01.950 --> 01:02:04.050
First, we shot in the

1337
01:02:04.050 --> 01:02:06.310
parking lot with Rain and Ed.

1338
01:02:06.670 --> 01:02:08.390
They performed the whole thing.

1339
01:02:08.390 --> 01:02:09.510
We shot it.

1340
01:02:09.690 --> 01:02:11.290
And the rest of us

1341
01:02:11.290 --> 01:02:17.490
were upstairs in Paul's office looking out that window and the camera could whip up to us.

1342
01:02:17.710 --> 01:02:18.730
In real time.

1343
01:02:18.910 --> 01:02:19.750
In real time.

1344
01:02:20.030 --> 01:02:20.190
Yes.

1345
01:02:20.190 --> 01:02:21.370
We watched all of it.

1346
01:02:21.830 --> 01:02:25.670
Then they moved the cameras up to Paul's office

1347
01:02:25.670 --> 01:02:30.890
to get really tight shots out of the window onto the action below,

1348
01:02:31.130 --> 01:02:34.010
and Rain and Ed had to do it all over again

1349
01:02:34.010 --> 01:02:37.070
just to get a few little shots through the window.

1350
01:02:37.290 --> 01:02:38.970
But then on a different day,

1351
01:02:39.190 --> 01:02:42.570
we shot inside the actual Dunder Mifflin conference room,

1352
01:02:42.610 --> 01:02:46.270
and this time we had to be careful to not shoot out the window

1353
01:02:46.270 --> 01:02:47.670
because there was nothing there.

1354
01:02:47.670 --> 01:02:48.730
It was just a backdrop.

1355
01:02:49.330 --> 01:02:52.150
And that we were basically looking at nothing,

1356
01:02:52.150 --> 01:02:56.230
but Dean was shouting out all the action that had happened the day before.

1357
01:02:57.090 --> 01:02:57.270
Right.

1358
01:02:57.630 --> 01:03:01.690
He said this was the moment when being an editor on the show really helped him.

1359
01:03:01.870 --> 01:03:06.590
He had kind of cut this whole thing together with a shot list inside his head,

1360
01:03:06.630 --> 01:03:10.190
and he just kept telling people, trust me, trust me, trust me, trust me.

1361
01:03:10.850 --> 01:03:12.470
He could see it, right?

1362
01:03:12.470 --> 01:03:13.450
He could see it.

1363
01:03:13.510 --> 01:03:14.670
He could see the whole thing.

1364
01:03:14.670 --> 01:03:21.470
He said he planned all of these whip pan cuts between the window, between us, all of it.

1365
01:03:21.470 --> 01:03:25.690
And when he got in the editing room, because he edited this episode as well,

1366
01:03:25.890 --> 01:03:30.630
it actually did all come together, and it looked really, really seamless.

1367
01:03:30.990 --> 01:03:33.730
Well, you have to think that Randy Cordray was like, I knew it.

1368
01:03:33.850 --> 01:03:34.550
I knew it.

1369
01:03:34.610 --> 01:03:34.930
Yes!

1370
01:03:35.110 --> 01:03:37.490
That Dean's editing was going to come into play here.

1371
01:03:37.630 --> 01:03:40.310
This is why Dean has to direct this episode.

1372
01:03:40.830 --> 01:03:43.610
But he did say it was a little grueling for the actors,

1373
01:03:43.610 --> 01:03:48.090
because we had to play these same moments over and over and over again,

1374
01:03:48.150 --> 01:03:49.810
more so than we normally do.

1375
01:03:49.810 --> 01:03:53.890
and we had to make it seem like we were doing it for the first time every time.

1376
01:03:54.370 --> 01:04:01.790
Now, as for the stunt, Randy told us that Ed actually drove the Prius silently through the

1377
01:04:01.790 --> 01:04:02.370
