1379
01:04:07.830 --> 01:04:13.410
They thought that they would have a stunt driver actually drive into a stunt Dwight.

1380
01:04:13.410 --> 01:04:14.110
Right.

1381
01:04:14.450 --> 01:04:19.850
And then after they were kind of squished, they would place Rain into the bushes.

1382
01:04:20.270 --> 01:04:21.790
And Ed into the car.

1383
01:04:21.950 --> 01:04:22.270
Yes.

1384
01:04:22.490 --> 01:04:27.830
But then on the commentary, didn't Rain say they just kind of ended up doing it themselves?

1385
01:04:28.590 --> 01:04:34.410
Actually, the commentary was Rainn Wilson, Jen Salata, Dean Holland, and Rusty Mahmood,

1386
01:04:34.490 --> 01:04:35.990
who was our first assistant director.

1387
01:04:36.470 --> 01:04:43.130
And they discussed that Ed actually drove into Rain very slowly.

1388
01:04:43.810 --> 01:04:46.090
And that it totally worked.

1389
01:04:46.410 --> 01:04:49.750
And those takes of those guys actually doing it were their favorite.

1390
01:04:49.970 --> 01:04:51.590
So those were the ones they used.

1391
01:04:51.730 --> 01:04:53.850
And they did not use takes with the stunt people.

1392
01:04:54.070 --> 01:05:00.490
Well, we also got a fan question from Samantha T who wanted to know what was up with the fence?

1393
01:05:00.750 --> 01:05:03.410
Like what was on the other side of it?

1394
01:05:03.550 --> 01:05:04.530
Was it padding?

1395
01:05:04.890 --> 01:05:06.730
Was it an actual fence?

1396
01:05:07.030 --> 01:05:09.430
Was the bumper of the car padded?

1397
01:05:09.730 --> 01:05:11.930
Was rain really being squashed?

1398
01:05:12.470 --> 01:05:18.910
Well, it was the real bumper of the car, and then Rain sent in an audio clip to tell us a little bit about the Bushes.

1399
01:05:19.390 --> 01:05:22.150
Oh, I'm so glad you guys are doing the duel.

1400
01:05:22.610 --> 01:05:24.610
Fantastic, one of my very favorite episodes.

1401
01:05:25.250 --> 01:05:30.970
And I always loved those episodes where Dwight and Andy got to go head to head.

1402
01:05:31.110 --> 01:05:38.510
I just loved that subplot of that tension, and Ed Helms is so funny in this episode.

1403
01:05:38.510 --> 01:05:46.230
But you know what it reminded me of is in college, we studied clowning and Commedia dell'Arte.

1404
01:05:46.570 --> 01:05:59.810
And it really is classic old, old comedy, like back from Commedia dell'Arte and the Greeks and ancient clowning of two idiots going at it over absurd s**t.

1405
01:06:00.310 --> 01:06:04.050
And in this case, Love and a Prius.

1406
01:06:04.250 --> 01:06:06.450
It was so much fun to shoot.

1407
01:06:06.450 --> 01:06:11.890
I don't remember a lot of specifics about it, but I remember the hedge had a lot of give in it,

1408
01:06:11.930 --> 01:06:14.510
so you could really pretend like you were pinned.

1409
01:06:15.050 --> 01:06:19.910
But it was just a big mass of vines, and it was actually very soft and comfortable.

1410
01:06:20.330 --> 01:06:23.610
And I love that line about the bears in Scranton.

1411
01:06:23.750 --> 01:06:24.830
It's so fantastic.

1412
01:06:25.630 --> 01:06:28.990
So I guess Rain was quite comfortable being pinned against the bushes.

1413
01:06:28.990 --> 01:06:29.730
No complaints.

1414
01:06:30.170 --> 01:06:32.710
Well, I can tell you about those big, giant hedges.

1415
01:06:32.710 --> 01:06:36.710
One time, Brian in a scene as Kevin nudged me

1416
01:06:36.710 --> 01:06:37.870
He thought it was a nudge

1417
01:06:37.870 --> 01:06:39.370
I went flying into them

1418
01:06:39.370 --> 01:06:41.030
I don't know if you remember that

1419
01:06:41.030 --> 01:06:42.430
I can't remember what episode

1420
01:06:42.430 --> 01:06:47.030
But I can attest to the fact that it's a very deep, dense

1421
01:06:48.790 --> 01:06:52.170
Very sort of a hedge you could fall into

1422
01:06:52.170 --> 01:06:54.250
Without getting to the other side

